{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1374958-a-guide-to-creature-building","id":1374958,"title":"A guide to Creature building?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-15T12:31:43-07:00","id":1374958,"title":"A guide to Creature building?","content":"I find nothing in the Hero book about how much Defense, Health and Initiative should be given to Creatures outside of a reference to the example antagonists chapter in the book. I have been all but useless at actually helping my players build their own creatures because I can make no sense out of how it's supposed to work.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to know what it would cost to apply Scale to something for the Creature. Would it too cost 2 dice just like any other Quality or Flair?<br /> <br /> Can someone help me find such guidelines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 03-15-2020, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T13:23:43-07:00","id":1374966,"title":"","content":"For creatures, the idea is to pick the already described creatures or antagonist templetes and make your own creature.<br /> <br /> My personal guidelines are:<br /> Rank 1 = Trivial<br /> Rank 2 = Foe<br /> Rank 3 = Rival<br /> Rank 4 = Nemesis<br /> Rank 5 = Titanspawn<br /> <br /> It will keep the Primary pool close to the rule (3 x rank) and give the other values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T13:27:26-07:00","id":1374967,"title":"","content":"Health - The Creature Rank. I think that's established somewhere.<br /> <br /> Defense - Followers get Rank/2, Rounded Up. I'd go with that for Creatures.<br /> <br /> Initiative - Eyeballing the Antagonist Rules, go with Primary Pool - 2, which is also what you'd probably do for establishing the Secondary Pool for the Creature.<br /> <br /> Scale - Technically Scale is a &quot;Thing that applies when it makes sense thing&quot;. Also, as I mentioned in the Relics thread: Scale be scary and I'd be wary of handing it out. At least at Hero level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T13:34:04-07:00","id":1374970,"title":"","content":"Initiative can be equal to Secondary or Desperation Pool, according to the focus of character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T23:11:35-07:00","id":1375019,"title":"","content":"The Hero Errata states in the FAQ section...<br /> <br /> Q) How much Health does a Creature start with?<br /> A) [Creature Birthright rating] x2. Creatures can also<br /> concede a confict and be Taken Out without filling all of their Health with Injuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25904-nika777","name":"nika777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T23:49:09-07:00","id":1375026,"title":"","content":"The Errata says Rating x 2, but I think that's slated to be changed because at Creature 3 you have 6 Injury Slots, and that's too damn many IMO. So I go with just Rating for Health Levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T06:43:44-07:00","id":1375076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1351117-deciding-creature-statistics?p=1359471#post1359471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It kind of is, unfortunately. I'd prefer to un-errata that and just go by what the book says.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on another thread where Neall chimed in, I would also echo NOT doing rating x2... it's just too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24323-zipdrive","name":"ZipDrive","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T04:19:47-07:00","id":1375253,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your answers!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1374958-a-guide-to-creature-building?p=1374967#post1374967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scale - Technically Scale is a &quot;Thing that applies when it makes sense thing&quot;. Also, as I mentioned in the Relics thread: Scale be scary and I'd be wary of handing it out. At least at Hero level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand that you should be wary of handling scale, but some vague guidelines would be appreciated. How would you handle a player who buys a Creature that should reasonably have scale in at least one aspect? For example if someone gets a nemean cheetah for the express purpose of it being able to run down anything that is not in a vehicle they probably expect their creature to have at least one level of scale in speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T12:23:27-07:00","id":1375311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1374958-a-guide-to-creature-building?p=1375253#post1375253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you all for your answers!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I understand that you should be wary of handling scale, but some vague guidelines would be appreciated. How would you handle a player who buys a Creature that should reasonably have scale in at least one aspect? For example if someone gets a nemean cheetah for the express purpose of it being able to run down anything that is not in a vehicle they probably expect their creature to have at least one level of scale in speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd cap any Hero tier Creature Scale at 1 or 2, tops. If the Heroes can't reach it themselves through Boons or Feats of Scale I wouldn't give them somethung that just exceeds that.<br /> <br /> So Scale 2 Speed is something I would feel is kind of the max for a Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T14:42:55-07:00","id":1375323,"title":"","content":"Id consider treating a scale increase as a flair.<br /> So take 1 in exchange for a few dices.<br /> Not sure how id treat an increase in size scale tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}